  "notes": ["Mountains and horizon mist -> NES rock browns at PC Engine lightness: darker and less orange than the NES rock.", "Sky keeps the PC Engine's pale gradient, so it is near-white 31/30 rather than the NES 21 blue (lighting rule).", "The cloud sea (row 1 entries 7-f) is 'cloud' (2C 3C 30); row 0 entries 9-b (light greys) are treated as cloud too.", "Vines/moss on the pillars (row 3 entries 9-b,d; row 4 b) have no NES counterpart: kept in the pillar role (greys/pink), so the vines become grey shading on plain NES-like pillars. Tried and rejected: cyan cloud column (teal pillars), rock browns (orange pillars).", "Rows 5/6 (statue, lamp, ornaments) use a 'mixed' role over the whole NES 2-2 palette."],
